# Normalise to LF in the repository and keep LF in the working tree.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf checks files out with CRLF on Windows while CI
# reads them as LF, so local checks disagree with CI in two ways this workspace
# has actually been bitten by:
#
#   - compliance.py hashes raw bytes, so every synced .compliance-kit/ file
#     reports KIT_FILE_HASH_MISMATCH locally while validating cleanly on Linux.
#   - a formatter whose default is LF (prettier, and dart format where CI pairs
#     it with `git diff --exit-code`) flags every file instead of the handful
#     that are genuinely misformatted, hiding the real ones in the noise.
#
# quorvyn_web has carried this rule since it was created; this brings the rest
# of the workspace in line.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.onnx binary
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
